**Then taste** the punishment, (fa-dhuqu), **for what you forgot** (bi-ma nasītum) **the meeting** (liqā'a) — meaning: for what you abandoned of the knowledge of the meeting of **this your day** (yawmikum hādhā), which is faith in it;

**Indeed We have forgotten you** (innā nasīnākum) — meaning: We have left you in the punishment like one who is forgotten;

**And taste the punishment of eternity** (wa-dhuqū ʿadhāba l-khuld) — i.e., the lasting punishment that has no cessation for it;

**for what you used to do** (bi-mā kuntum taʿmalūn), of disbelief and sins.
